From bb12f3f8b97a6f6f2be8b4318b0dcec7cb622393 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:42:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/49] Red team fix 6: files kept from the lock wait are
 compared by size too, and check keeps nothing

What a command read during the lock's settle delay was kept when the files
were still listed under the same names after the lock was confirmed. A name
is the hash of what was read; it says nothing about what is stored under it
now. An index file cut short or changed in place before confirmation kept
its name, and check, whose index pass was prepared during the delay, reported
a repository as healthy that stock reports as damaged.

(a) Every file kept from the wait must now be listed, after confirmation,
with the size it was listed with when it was read: the index files of
backup, restore, ls, forget and prune (the index remembers the listed size
of each file it loaded), and the one snapshot file ls reads ahead. Another
size discards everything read during the wait, and the command reads again
as stock does and reports what stock reports. Damage that leaves the length
alone is not seen by these commands without reading the file again; stock
reads index files through the cache and does not see it either unless the
cache is off.

(b) check starts no reads during the delay any more. It takes stock's lock
call and reads snapshots and index after confirmation, in stock's order. The
pack sizes implied by the index are still computed once for the pack pass
and the read-data pass. The wait work of check, its tests and the checker's
LoadSnapshotsFromList are removed.

Tests: TestCheckReportsIndexDamagedBeforeLockConfirmation is the reviewers'
scenario (seat 1 R1, seat 2 finding 2) at the level of the command with the
production 200 ms delay, for an index cut short and for a same-size bit
flip, with and without cache: all four fail before this commit (check
returns success) and pass after, with the error of a check run after the
damage. The reviewers' two lifecycle tests drove check's wait work
directly, which no longer exists. TestLockWaitReadsRejectResizedIndexFile
(fails before) and TestPreparedSnapshotKeptOnlyWithListedSize cover (a).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
